{"sections":[],"kind":"article","metadata":{"title":"Privacy Manifests","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"],"title":"Choosing what to record"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"type":"text","text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"type":"text","text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Required-reason APIs","anchor":"Required-reason-APIs"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), system boot time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), disk space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), active keyboards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and user defaults","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). The modules that come nearest:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Module"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"swift-system’s "},{"code":"FileDescriptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"read","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"write","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"resize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"close","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"unlink","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"FileManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"createDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"setAttributes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the file protection class), "},{"code":"contentsOfDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"isExcludedFromBackup","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from ","type":"text"},{"code":"stat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset ","type":"text"},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"ide